<form method="post" action="CryptoCustody.php" class="card p-3 mb-3"><h2 class="h5">Inspect one deposit-record page (evidence only)</h2><p>Checks the selected account UID before and after one authenticated page query. At most five records, a past window of at most 24 hours, TRX/USDT on TRON only. Mixed/unsupported networks or malformed rows refuse the entire page. This is not complete history, an importer or scheduled polling. No checkpoint advances and no funds are credited. Records and opaque cursors are encrypted; only the evidence digest is returned here. No provider calls occur on page load.</p><?php $target();?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="inspect_deposit_page"><label>Source vendor credential configuration ID<input class="form-control" name="source_vendor_id" inputmode="numeric" required></label><label>Coin<select class="form-select" name="coin"><option value="USDT">USDT:TRX</option><option value="TRX">TRX:TRX</option></select></label><label>Start UTC Unix milliseconds (13 digits ending 000)<input class="form-control" name="start_ms" pattern="[1-9][0-9]{9}000" maxlength="13" inputmode="numeric" required></label><label>End UTC Unix milliseconds (later than start, not in future)<input class="form-control" name="end_ms" pattern="[1-9][0-9]{9}000" maxlength="13" inputmode="numeric" required></label><label>Optional opaque cursor from protected evidence (same query window only; no progress is committed)<textarea class="form-control" name="cursor" maxlength="2048" autocomplete="off"></textarea></label><?php $security();?><button class="btn btn-outline-primary mt-2">Inspect one page and store encrypted evidence</button></form>
<form method="post" action="CryptoCustody.php" class="card p-3 mb-3"><h2 class="h5">Protected polling conflict review</h2><p>Audited metadata-only health and conflict report: at most 20 streams with advisory recovery actions and 100 recent lease events per stream, plus 50 recent sightings and 10 competing identity pairs per sighting. Truncation is explicit. Includes original classification and current conflict state, which can change as later evidence arrives. Hashes are sensitive correlation metadata. This report does not decrypt records, resolve conflicts, reset streams, clear holds or authorize imports/credits. Use protected evidence review separately to inspect a referenced evidence digest. Use Stop below to halt a stream; stale or expired streams must not be reset or silently rebound.</p><?php $target();?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="review_poll"><?php $security();?><button class="btn btn-outline-primary mt-2">Open audited health and conflict report</button></form>
<form method="post" action="CryptoCustody.php" class="card p-3 mb-3"><h2 class="h5">Acknowledge retry escalation alert</h2><p>Use the stream ID and alert revision from a fresh protected report. Acknowledgement records only who saw the alert: it does not resolve failures, clear retry escalation, reset a cursor or permit funds movement. Alerts are local records, not delivered email/SMS notifications.</p><?php $target();?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="ack_poll_alert"><label>Stream ID<input name="stream_id" class="form-control" pattern="[a-f0-9]{32}" maxlength="32" required></label><label>Alert revision<input name="alert_revision" class="form-control" inputmode="numeric" required></label><?php $security();?><button class="btn btn-outline-primary mt-2">Record acknowledgement only</button></form>
